  "bc_choice": "option (b), a genuinely moving top boundary: cells with z >= z_face+delta are pinned to c_bulk every step (row elimination on the FiPy matrix).  The quasi-steady flux matches platesim's delta-plane Dirichlet, but NOT exactly: the pin sits on the first cell row at or above the plane, so the effective plane is 0-1 dx above platesim's, i.e. 0-6.25 % (mean 0.5 dx = 2 um, 3.1 %) of delta = 64 um at dx 4.  Because the flux scales as 1/delta, that perturbs the surface concentration by ~(j/j_lim)*(0-6.25 %) <~0.7 % of c_bulk (mean ~0.4 %), and floor/field by a few 1e-3.  It is the leading known boundary-condition discretisation term of this comparison, not negligible by construction",
  "fipy_version": "4.0.3",
  "notes": [
   "FiPy 4.0.3 does not apply CellVariable cell constraints to the linear system (fipy/variables/variable.py only masks .value), so the moving Dirichlet is imposed by row elimination instead of var.constrain(...)",
   "D_face uses platesim's smeared Hs = 0.5(1+tanh(phi/1.2dx)) (fields.py StepGeom.Hs); the upstream sharp _LevelSetDiffusionVariable isolates solid-side interface cells and the implicit sink then drains them to c=0"
  ],
